// Stress question: at what population does a sustained seeking flood fall behind?
// Start empty. 64 sources each emit once per tick: 3,840 bodies per sim second.
// At 60Hz the 32,768 cap arrives after 512 ticks (8.53 simulation seconds).
// Wall time grows when the simulation cannot keep up. Watch population / tick,
// not just apparent FPS. Kite, select Crowd breaker in F1, and clear pockets.
// Every source counts the same population before this tick's drain. The cap is
// a multiple of 64, so it lands exactly with no attacks; kills may permit a
// final batch to overshoot the threshold by at most 63 (it is a source gate).
// 8 x 8 nests, 8m apart, each spreading arrivals over a 2m ring. No source
// starts on the player. Sources keep refilling after kills below the threshold.
(
    name: "Stress - 64 spawners to 32,768 seekers",
    sources: [
        (pos: (-28.0, -28.0), radius: 2.0, every: 1, when: FewerThan(32768), what: (seeks: true)),
        (pos: (-20.0, -28.0), radius: 2.0, every: 1, when: FewerThan(32768), what: (seeks: true)),
